# CITATION.cff for testpick — commit at the repo root as CITATION.cff
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: testpick
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-21
authors:
  - family-names: Sampathi
    given-names: Shiva
repository-code: https://github.com/agentbantu-wq/testpick
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Run only the tests your change can actually affect. A Go CLI that reads
  the files a change touches and proposes exactly which test suites CI
  should run: by file-name convention, by same-package tests, and by
  walking the reverse import graph, so a change to a deep dependency
  selects the tests of everything that depends on it, transitively. New
  test files get a suggested rerun count, so flaky tests get shaken out
  before they block a merge. Deterministic and local-only: no LLM, no
  network, no test execution.
keywords:
  - continuous-integration
  - testing
  - test-selection
  - go
  - site-reliability-engineering
